Aerie-Purpose: Offer DuckDuckGo (the default), Brave, Kagi and Startpage as the built-in search engines, and no Google, Bing, Ecosia or Qwant.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/search_engines_data/resources/definitions/regional_settings.json (default "ZZ" list)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Helium already makes the "ZZ" list the only one and falls back to DuckDuckGo
(search/engine-defaults.patch); this patch trims that list. A custom engine,
SearXNG for example, uses the existing custom search engine feature (see
docs/search.md). Search suggestions are off by default in Helium
(inox-patchset/modify-default-prefs.patch); the source gates check both.

--- a/third_party/search_engines_data/resources/definitions/regional_settings.json
+++ b/third_party/search_engines_data/resources/definitions/regional_settings.json
@@ -135,13 +135,9 @@
       // Default
       "search_engines": [
           "&duckduckgo",
-          "&ecosia",
-          "&bing",
-          "&break_stuff_google",
-          "&qwant",
+          "&brave",
           "&kagi",
-          "&startpage",
-          "&brave"
+          "&startpage"
       ]
     }
   },
